# Northstar payments rules

- Never post to the legacy ledger more than once for the same logical payment.
- Prefer explicit error codes (`order_not_found`, `conflict`, `ledger_unavailable`) over free-form Error messages.
- Any new mutating payments API must accept an `Idempotency-Key` (header or body) and be safe under client retries.
- Update `openapi.yaml` in the same change as handler behavior.
- Add or update tests for happy path + replay + ledger failure.
- Do not invent on-prem mainframe access — keep the `LegacyLedgerClient` boundary.
